 "note": "Two bowls (home rings) pinched into a waist of K 30 junctions (mirror). A rotor at the top and bottom of the waist joins the two K arms through the neck (r1) or the bowls' rims over the shoulders (r2): the crossing always exists, but it jumps between the neck and the rims. [KEEP edit 2026-11-11: the long bridge between the two platforms next to each home (BU - BD) is a ferry; the waist switches stay.]",
 "geometricSymmetry": true,
 "labVariant": {
  "junctions": true
 },
 "experimental": true,
 "ruleWaivers": {
  "N13": "rotor -> switch (rulebook pass 2026-10-28): the two states join decks of different tiers / spacing, which N13 forbids for a rigid rotor; the connections per state are the original's",
  "N03": "the switch hub IS the crossing by design (every state keeps 2+ decks, so the game's _islands counts its decks as fixed and never strands a side); N03 reads 'relays only add shortcuts' - Daniele's call on hub crossings"
 },
